{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975785,"nonce":"YFiuSRVNfpUuZ8oEykQCpqkg4+o=","title":"CallMethod's slot fall-through is silent, and Cranelift may share the own-list assumption","message":"The LLVM `CallMethod` object path resolved a slot's `pindex` against the\nreceiver's OWN proto list; a subclass's list holds only what it declares, so a\ncall through a subclass-typed receiver to an inherited method found nothing and\nfell into a path that called nothing. Fixed by walking the super chain.\n\nTwo follow-ups:\n  1. the fall-through path must never be silent -- make it throw or trap, so the\n     next slot mismatch is a crash with a name rather than a no-op;\n  2. audit the Cranelift tier's `CallMethod` for the same own-list assumption.\n     Hybrid never showed the symptom only because the affected body ran\n     interpreted.","files":null}]}